AIM
To design and develop a static web page using HTML and CSS with a header, navigation menu, content sections and footer.

PROGRAM
Save the following code as 1.html and open it in a web browser.

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>My Static Web Page</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            background-color: #f2f2f2;
            margin: 0;
        }
        header {
            background-color: #333;
            color: white;
            text-align: center;
            padding: 25px;
        }
        nav {
            background-color: #555;
            text-align: center;
            padding: 15px;
        }
        nav a {
            color: white;
            text-decoration: none;
            margin: 15px;
        }
        .container {
            width: 85%;
            margin: 30px auto;
            display: flex;
            gap: 20px;
        }
        .box {
            background-color: white;
            padding: 25px;
            flex: 1;
            text-align: center;
            border-radius: 8px;
        }
        footer {
            background-color: #333;
            color: white;
            text-align: center;
            padding: 15px;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <header>
        <h1>Welcome to My Web Page</h1>
        <p>Static Web Page Using HTML and CSS</p>
    </header>

    <nav>
        <a href="#">Home</a>
        <a href="#">About</a>
        <a href="#">Services</a>
        <a href="#">Contact</a>
    </nav>

    <div class="container">
        <div class="box">
            <h2>HTML</h2>
            <p>HTML is used to create the structure of a webpage.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="box">
            <h2>CSS</h2>
            <p>CSS is used to add colours, fonts and styles.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="box">
            <h2>Web Design</h2>
            <p>HTML and CSS help create attractive web pages.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <footer>
        <p>Copyright 2026 - My Web Page</p>
    </footer>
</body>
</html>

OUTPUT
The browser displays a static webpage containing:
1. A header with the page title and description.
2. A navigation bar with Home, About, Services and Contact links.
3. Three content boxes for HTML, CSS and Web Design.
4. A footer with copyright information.

RESULT
Thus, a static web page was successfully designed using HTML and CSS.
